On the DS parameterization a second expansion gives `W=378\lambda^7`, the displayed `f^3-g^2`, and resultant `(3^9 7^2/2^5)\lambda^{27}`, the last obtained twice. For `lambda\neq 0` there is no persistent common root. The tautology `f H'-3f'H=-Wg` identifies a nonzero constant Wronskian at degrees `(6,9)` with an extremal order-three DS pair. Under `a_4=4lambda` one has `(189/8192)a_4^7=378\lambda^7`.

